# * holdings --chart and svg output

<
commodity AAPL ; lots:
commodity XYZ ; lots:
commodity NEW ; lots:
commodity SAP ; lots:
account revenues:gains ; type: G
commodity 1,000.00 USD
commodity 1.000,00 EUR

account assets:broker   ; type: A
account assets:eu       ; type: A

2024-01-10 buy
  assets:broker    10 AAPL @ 150 USD
  assets:cash

2024-02-10 buy
  assets:broker    20 XYZ @ 50 USD
  assets:cash

2024-03-10 buy
  assets:broker    5 NEW @ 20 USD
  assets:cash

2024-03-15 buy
  assets:eu        30 SAP @ 100 EUR
  assets:cash

2024-06-01 sell some
  assets:broker    -5 XYZ @ 60 USD
  assets:cash   300 USD
  revenues:gains

P 2024-12-31 AAPL 250 USD
P 2024-12-31 XYZ 30 USD
P 2024-12-31 SAP 120 EUR

# ** 1. A holding is charted as its cost and its unrealised gain, reaching its value (shown);
# or with an unrealised loss, as the part of its cost it is worth and the part lost, reaching its cost.
# A holding without a market price is charted as its cost, in a muted colour, with no value.
# Since a value is not always the end of its bar, the values are also marked.
# There is a panel per commodity.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 --chart -w 70
Holdings on 2024-12-31

USD
█ Cost  ▒ Unrealised gain  ╱ Unrealised loss  ▓ No market price
┃ Value

assets:broker AAPL  2,500.00 USD  ██████████████████████▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒┃
assets:broker NEW                 ▓
assets:broker XYZ     450.00 USD  █████┃╱╱╱╱╱

EUR
█ Cost  ▒ Unrealised gain

assets:eu SAP  3.600,00 EUR  ██████████████████████████████████▒▒▒▒▒▒▒

# ** 2. With --lots, each lot is charted, labelled by account, commodity and lot.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 --lots --chart -w 110
Holdings on 2024-12-31

USD
█ Cost  ▒ Unrealised gain  ╱ Unrealised loss  ▓ No market price  ┃ Value

assets:broker AAPL {2024-01-10, 15..  2,500.00 USD  ███████████████████████████████████▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒┃
assets:broker XYZ {2024-02-10, 50...    450.00 USD  █████████┃╱╱╱╱╱╱╱
assets:broker NEW {2024-03-10, 20...                ▓▓

EUR
█ Cost  ▒ Unrealised gain

assets:eu SAP {2024-03-15, 100,00 ..  3.600,00 EUR  ████████████████████████████████████████████████▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒▒

# ** 3. A chart of only holdings without a market price (eg with -X and no exchange rate) still has a legend, explaining their colour.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 -X EUR --chart -w 60 broker
Holdings on 2024-12-31

█ No market price

assets:broker AAPL  ████████████████████████████████████████
assets:broker NEW   ██▋
assets:broker XYZ   ████████████████████

# ** 4. In SVG, the bars are coloured as an asset (cost), revenue (gain) and expense (loss), and the values are shown above them.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 -O svg broker | grep -o 'class="fill [a-z0-9]*"\|class="value"[^>]*>[^<]*' | sed 's/class="value"[^>]*>//' | sort -u
2,500.00 USD
450.00 USD
class="fill other"
class="fill ta0"
class="fill tr0"
class="fill tx0"

# ** 5. In SVG, the part lost is hatched (here, one holding's, and its legend swatch).
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 -O svg broker | grep -c 'fill="url(#hledger-chart-hatch)"'
2

# ** 6. With csv output, --chart gives the chart's data: each series' value per holding.
$ hledger -f- holdings -e 2025-01-01 --chart -O csv eu
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"EUR","Cost","item","bar","assets:eu SAP","3000,00"
"EUR","Unrealised gain","item","bar","assets:eu SAP","600,00"
"EUR","Value","total","marker","assets:eu SAP","3600,00"
